{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSTcC3zgD71uhum1BhA2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository has (from inspection):**\n\n1. **Error handling**: Exceptions are thrown from controllers/services and caught by `GlobalExceptionHandler`. Status codes come from the exception type:\n   - `ResourceNotFoundException` → 404\n   - `ConflictException` → 409\n   - `ValidationException` → 400\n\n2. **Status transitions**: When a shipment is created, it gets `ShipmentStatus.CREATED` (line 40 in ShipmentController.kt)\n\n3. **Request/response pattern**: POST endpoints return `ResponseEntity<T>` with explicit status; GET endpoints return the object directly\n\n4. **Tests**: Use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions; the error envelope is checked as `$.error.code`\n\n5. **State branching**: Per the knowledge router, exhaustive `when` expressions should be used for enum cases (no `else` clause), so the compiler enforces all states are handled\n\n**Affected files** (expected to change):\n\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Add error code for \"shipment cannot be confirmed in current state\" (for CANCELLED rejection). Cannot be avoided as the ticket requires 409 rejection with an error code.\n\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add the confirm endpoint. Cannot be avoided as this is the main requirement.\n\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add tests for all four cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED idempotent, CANCELLED→409, missing→404). Cannot be avoided as acceptance criteria require tested behavior.\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- **Immutability**: Shipment is a data class. Need to use `.copy(status = ...)` to create a modified instance.\n- **Concurrent state changes**: In-memory repository doesn't protect against race conditions, but the ticket doesn't require it.\n- **Error code naming**: Must be consistent with existing patterns (all caps, descriptive). I'll use `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED`.\n\n**Open questions:**\n\nNone that affect correctness—the ticket is clear on all four cases and their expected outcomes.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **`sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt`**\n   - Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This covers the case where a shipment is in `CANCELLED` status and cannot transition to `CONFIRMED`.\n\n2. **`sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt`**\n   - Add a new method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>` with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` annotation.\n   - The method should:\n     - Look up the shipment by ID; throw `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found\n     - Use an exhaustive `when` on `shipment.status` to handle all three cases:\n       - `CREATED`: transition to `CONFIRMED`, save and return\n       - `CONFIRMED`: return unchanged (idempotent)\n       - `CANCELLED`: throw `ConflictException` with the new error code\n     - Return `ResponseEntity.ok(updatedShipment)` in all success cases\n\n3. **`sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`**\n   - Add four new tests:\n     - `confirms a created shipment` — create shipment, confirm it, verify status is `CONFIRMED`\n     - `idempotently confirms an already confirmed shipment` — create and confirm, then confirm again, verify no error and status remains `CONFIRMED`\n     - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409` — create shipment, manually set status to `CANCELLED` in repo, attempt confirm, verify 409 and error code\n     - `rejects confirming a missing shipment with 404` — attempt confirm on non-existent ID, verify 404 and error code\n\n**Alternative approaches rejected:**\n\n1. **Use a service layer for the state transition logic** — The existing controllers (OrderController, ShipmentController for create/get) do not use a service layer; they call the repository directly. Consistency dictates staying with that pattern.\n\n2. **Create a separate `ConfirmShipmentRequest` class** — The confirm operation needs only the shipment ID (from path), not a request body, so this is unnecessary.\n\n3. **Use an `if/else if` chain instead of `when`** — Rejected per the knowledge base: exhaustive `when` in expression position is required to ensure all status cases are handled and future enum additions force a compilation error.\n\n4. **Return 400 (ValidationException) instead of 409 for CANCELLED** — The ticket explicitly says \"409\", and it correctly models that as a conflict (the resource exists but is in a conflicting state), not a validation error (malformed input).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | HTTP Path | Status Before | Logic | Status After | Response | HTTP |\n|------|-----------|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Confirm CREATED | POST `/shipments/S-1/confirm` | CREATED | Update in-memory store | CONFIRMED | Shipment object | 200 |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED | POST `/shipments/S-1/confirm` | CONFIRMED | No-op (idempotent) | CONFIRMED | Shipment object | 200 |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | POST `/shipments/S-1/confirm` | CANCELLED | Throw ConflictException | (unchanged) | Error envelope with code | 409 |\n| Confirm missing | POST `/shipments/missing/confirm` | (doesn't exist) | Throw ResourceNotFoundException | (N/A) | Error envelope with code | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **`confirms a created shipment`** — Covers acceptance criterion 3 (confirm persists); verifies the basic state transition.\n\n2. **`idempotently confirms already confirmed`** — Covers acceptance criterion 5 (retry succeeds); ensures idempotency.\n\n3. **`rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409`** — Covers acceptance criterion 5 (cancelled rejected); verifies error code and status.\n\n4. **`rejects confirming a missing shipment with 404`** — Covers acceptance criterion 5 (unknown ID rejected); verifies error code and status.\n\nAll tests validate the error envelope via `$.error.code` to ensure error responses are consistent with the rest of the API (criterion 4).\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nI'll now implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":722,"cache_read_input_tokens":21735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":722},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b84cb12d-d6bf-4d8a-b8a1-7dbe586553b9","uuid":"cd9eefca-1994-48dd-9e3c-73aafebaf708","timestamp":"2026-09-26T17:39:29.515Z","request_id":"req_011CfSTcBgQZqYG44i79GkGa"}
